To solve this problem, we can model it as a graph traversal problem where each index in the array represents a node, and there is an edge between two nodes if the greatest common divisor (gcd) of their corresponding values is greater than 1. The task is to determine if every pair of nodes is connected directly or indirectly (i.e., there's a path between them).

For this to be true, the graph must be connected. We can use a union-find data structure (also known as a disjoint set data structure) to keep track of connected components in the graph. The idea is to group nodes that are directly connected, and if all nodes are in a single group after processing all edges, then the graph is connected, and we return `True`. Otherwise, we return `False`.

